===Etymology 1===
{{PIE word|en|dwóh₁}}
From {{inh|en|enm|devisen}}, {{m|enm|devysen}}, from {{der|en|fro|deviser}}, from {{der|en|VL.|devisō}}, from {{der|en|la|dīvisō}}, frequentative of {{m|la|dīvidō}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To use one’s [[intellect]] to [[plan]] or [[design]] (something).
#: {{ux|en|to '''devise''' an argument; to '''devise''' a machine, or a new system of writing}}
#* {{RQ:Skelton Complete|Hauke|62|lines=20–23|Therefore to make complaynt<br>Of such mysadvysed<br>Parsons and dysgysed,<br>Thys boke we have '''devysed''', {{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:Marlowe Tamburlaine|part=1|scene=ii|page=25|passage=His fiery eies are fixt vpon the earth.<br>As if he now '''deuiſ’d''' some Stratageme:<br>Or meant to pierce ''Auernus'' darkſome vauts.<br>To pull the triple headed dog from hell.}}
#* {{RQ:Bancroft United States
|passage='''devising''' schemes to realize his ambitious views}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1988|author=Andrew Radford| title=Transformational Grammar| location=Cambridge| publisher=University Press| page=23| isbn=0-521-34750-5| passage=Thus, the task of the linguist '''devising''' a grammar which models the linguistic competence of the fluent native speaker is to '''devise''' a ''finite'' set of rules which are capable of specifying how to form, interpret, and pronounce an ''infinite'' set of well-formed sentences.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.reuters.com/article/us-thailand-election-rules-explainer/numbers-game-how-thailands-election-system-favors-pro-army-parties-idUSKCN1R20OV| title=Numbers game: How Thailand's election system favors pro-army parties| date=2019-03-21| accessdate=2019-03-23| work=Reuters| publisher=Reuters| author=Setboonsarg, Chayut; Johnson, Kay| editor=Robert Birsel| text=Thailand goes to the polls on Sunday under a new system that critics say the military government has '''devised''' to prevent the most popular political party, which has won every election since 2001, from returning to power.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[leave]] ([[property]]) in a [[will]].
# {{lb|en|intransitive|archaic}} To form a scheme; to lay a plan; to contrive; to consider.
#* {{RQ:Homer Pope et al Odyssey|book=IX|passage=I thought, '''devised''', and Pallas heard my prayer.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|archaic}} To plan or scheme for; to plot to obtain.
#* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|book=VI|canto=IX|stanza=30|passage=For wisedome is most riches; fooles therefore / They are, which fortunes doe by vowes '''deuize''',}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} To [[imagine]]; to [[guess]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Romeo and Juliet|3|1|passage=I do protest I neuer iniur’d thee, <br>But lou’d thee better then thou can’st '''deuise''': <br>Till thou shalt know the reason of my loue.}}

